L-f is implemented and every lane ran. On each fast lane the only failure is the known `yin.vm.ucf.handoff-v2-census-test` baseline (missing `handoff-v2.txt`). Nothing is staged or committed; the slice is waiting for review and Architect sign-off. The full report is at `collab/1791406000000-engineer-l-f.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md`.

**What changed**
- **R1/R2 (bounds):** `default-bounds` now allows 65536 parts (depth 256 and 16 MiB unchanged). `publish-module!` takes `{:bounds ...}` and passes it to both closure walks and every `link-local`; `link-local` passes it to its runtime.
- **R3 (derivation tree):** the `:verifying` policy now fetches the manifest's tree through steps 2 to 4 only and never scans it. This adds the optional request key `:yin.link/scan? false` and a five-argument `verify`. Ordinary links behave as before. A requested tree image still scans (decision L1), and a test checks both cases by counting scanner calls.
- **R4, and R5 because the measurements required it:** all three tree scanners are now one walk over the occurrence relation, and the old Datalog query scanners are deleted. Conformance tests hold each scanner equal to its Datalog definition on 20 fixtures plus a small wide-layout module. One fixture is the shared row bound at one place and free at another; it yields exactly one record, at the free place.
- **R6:** `yin.repl.link/composition` takes `:derivation` (default `:verifying`), and `attempt` forwards it. An `:ok` response now carries `:derivation` and `:trust`.
- **Design docs:** all the §5.4 edits are made. I also added `:yin.link/scan?` to the documented closed key set in §6.3 of `yin.vm.linker.md`, which §5.4 did not list.

